<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>Class: Assembly Process</title>
  <style>
    body {
      font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
      margin: 40px;
      line-height: 1.6;
    }
    h1, h2 {
      color: #2a4d8f;
    }
    .section {
      margin-bottom: 25px;
    }
    .code {
      background: #f4f4f4;
      padding: 6px 10px;
      border-radius: 4px;
      font-family: monospace;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <h1>Class: Assembly Process</h1>

  <div class="section">
    <strong>Label:</strong> Assembly Process
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <strong>Definition:</strong>  
    <p>
      Manufacturing process in which a number of material components are physically connected to each other to form an assembly.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <strong>Subclass of:</strong>  
    <span class="code">ManufacturingProcess</span>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <strong>Rationale:</strong>  
    <p>
      More conditions (differentia) need to be agreed upon by the domain experts as processes like 3D printing can also produce an assembly.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <strong>SKOS Example:</strong>
    <ul>
      <li>Driving a lug nut to hold the wheel of a car in place</li>
      <li>Welding two metal parts into a single object</li>
      <li>Automated drilling and riveting of a skin panel operation during fuselage assembly</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

</body>
</html>

